// Scenario 5. tovrin. A red case is not run without orch's flip; a counterexample that is a printout of Haskell
// values is refuted; a run more than a tenth over its bound violates `Owes-Time-Bound`.
// The rules of tovrin.ratchet, tovrin.cex (with std.rails 1) and tovrin.budgets, by hand in the reference eFLINT
// that eflint-rs reads. Whether a text holds a dump mark is `matches_glob`, a host function eflint-rs does not
// have: its answer is given as a fact here (`has-dump-mark`), and runs for real in the docket-v2 script. Every
// query must succeed.
Fact party Identified by String
Fact role-name Identified by String
Fact role Identified by party * role-name
Fact family Identified by String
Fact of-family Identified by party * family
Fact other-family Identified by party * party'
  Holds when (Exists family, family' : of-family(party, family) && of-family(party', family') && family != family')
Fact verifier-module Identified by party
Fact case Identified by String
Fact suite Identified by String
Fact run Identified by String
Fact in-suite Identified by case * suite
Fact red-case Identified by case
Fact flip-requested Identified by case
Fact blocked-suite Identified by suite
  Holds when (Exists case : in-suite(case, suite) && red-case(case) && Not(flip-requested(case)))
Fact suite-run Identified by suite * run
Act flip-case
  Actor party
  Related to case
  Holds when role(party, "orch") && red-case(case) && Not(flip-requested(case))
  Creates flip-requested(case)
Act run-proof-suite
  Actor party
  Related to suite, run
  Holds when role(party, "runner") && Not(blocked-suite(suite))
  Creates suite-run(suite, run)
Event case-ran-red
  Related to case
  Creates red-case(case)
  Terminates flip-requested(case)

Fact artifact Identified by String
Fact condition Identified by String
Fact assigned Identified by party * artifact
Fact given-by Identified by artifact * party
Fact counterexample-artifact Identified by artifact
Fact has-dump-mark Identified by artifact              // stands for matches_glob(text, "*MkForest*") and the like
Fact required Identified by artifact * condition
  Holds when counterexample-artifact(artifact)
             && (condition == condition("valid_tovrin_p4_syntax") || condition == condition("no_raw_haskell_ast_dump"))
Fact claimed-done Identified by party * artifact
Fact verified Identified by artifact * condition
Fact refuted Identified by artifact * condition
Fact all-verified Identified by artifact
  Holds when (Exists party : claimed-done(party, artifact))
             && Not(Exists condition : required(artifact, condition) && Not(verified(artifact, condition)))
Fact shown-violated Identified by artifact
  Holds when counterexample-artifact(artifact) && all-verified(artifact)
Fact may-find Identified by party * party' * artifact
  Holds when (Exists party'' : claimed-done(party'', artifact) && Not(assigned(party', artifact))
              && ((role(party, "owner") && party' == party)
                  || (verifier-module(party) && role(party', "looker") && other-family(party', party''))))
Duty owes-valid-result
  Holder party
  Claimant party'
  Related to artifact, condition
  Holds when assigned(party, artifact) && given-by(artifact, party') && required(artifact, condition) && Not(verified(artifact, condition))
  Violated when refuted(artifact, condition)
Act claim-done
  Actor party
  Related to artifact
  Holds when assigned(party, artifact) && (Exists condition : required(artifact, condition))
  Creates claimed-done(party, artifact)
Act verify-condition
  Actor party
  Related to party', artifact, condition
  Holds when may-find(party, party', artifact) && required(artifact, condition)
  Creates verified(artifact, condition)
  Terminates refuted(artifact, condition)
Act refute-condition
  Actor party
  Related to party', artifact, condition
  Holds when may-find(party, party', artifact) && required(artifact, condition)
  Creates refuted(artifact, condition)
  Terminates verified(artifact, condition)
  Terminates claimed-done(party'', artifact) When claimed-done(party'', artifact)

Fact figure Identified by String
Fact amount Identified by Int
Fact baseline Identified by case * figure * amount
Fact measured Identified by case * figure * amount
Fact overruled Identified by case * figure
Fact regressed Identified by case * figure
  Holds when (Exists amount, amount' : baseline(case, figure, amount) && measured(case, figure, amount')
              && amount' * 10 > amount * 11) && Not(overruled(case, figure))
Duty owes-time-bound
  Holder party
  Claimant party'
  Related to case, figure
  Holds when role(party, "runner") && role(party', "owner")
             && (Exists amount : baseline(case, figure, amount)) && (Exists amount : measured(case, figure, amount))
  Violated when regressed(case, figure)
Event case-measured-green
  Related to case, figure, amount
  Terminates measured(case, figure, amount') When measured(case, figure, amount')
  Terminates baseline(case, figure, amount') When baseline(case, figure, amount') && amount < amount'
  Creates measured(case, figure, amount)
  Creates baseline(case, figure, amount) When Not(Exists amount' : baseline(case, figure, amount') && amount' <= amount)
Act overrule-bound
  Actor party
  Related to case, figure
  Holds when role(party, "owner") || role(party, "orch")
  Creates overruled(case, figure)
.
+party("o1"). +party("or1"). +party("tovrin.runner"). +party("b1"). +party("tovrin.cex"). 
+role-name("owner"). +role-name("orch"). +role-name("runner"). +role-name("looker").
+role("o1", "owner"). +role("or1", "orch"). +role("tovrin.runner", "runner"). +role("tovrin.cex", "looker").
+family("anthropic"). +family("machine"). +of-family("b1", "anthropic"). +of-family("tovrin.cex", "machine").
+verifier-module("tovrin.cex").
+case("lemma-3"). +suite("proofs"). +in-suite("lemma-3", "proofs"). +run("r1"). +run("r2").

// 1. The ratchet: a red case is not run by anything until orch flips it, and one flip lets one run.
case-ran-red("lemma-3").
?!Enabled(run-proof-suite("tovrin.runner", "proofs", "r1")).    // the runner itself is refused: nothing runs it automatically
?!Enabled(run-proof-suite("b1", "proofs", "r1")).
?!Enabled(flip-case("b1", "lemma-3")).                     // nobody but orch flips
?!Enabled(flip-case("tovrin.runner", "lemma-3")).
flip-case("or1", "lemma-3").
run-proof-suite("tovrin.runner", "proofs", "r1").
case-ran-red("lemma-3").
?!Enabled(run-proof-suite("tovrin.runner", "proofs", "r2")).    // the flip was for one run

// 2. A counterexample that is a printout of Haskell values.
+artifact("cex-17"). +artifact("cex-18").
+condition("valid_tovrin_p4_syntax"). +condition("no_raw_haskell_ast_dump").
+counterexample-artifact("cex-17"). +assigned("b1", "cex-17"). +given-by("cex-17", "or1").
+has-dump-mark("cex-17").                                       // its text holds `MkForest`
claim-done("b1", "cex-17").
refute-condition("tovrin.cex", "tovrin.cex", "cex-17", "no_raw_haskell_ast_dump").
?Violated(owes-valid-result("b1", "or1", "cex-17", "no_raw_haskell_ast_dump")).
?!shown-violated("cex-17").                                     // the violation it claims counts for nothing
?!Enabled(verify-condition("b1", "tovrin.cex", "cex-17", "no_raw_haskell_ast_dump")).   // not by the builder, in the replay's name

// 3. One in Tovrin's own P4 syntax, which the replay ran and saw break the property.
+counterexample-artifact("cex-18"). +assigned("b1", "cex-18"). +given-by("cex-18", "or1").
claim-done("b1", "cex-18").
verify-condition("tovrin.cex", "tovrin.cex", "cex-18", "no_raw_haskell_ast_dump").
verify-condition("tovrin.cex", "tovrin.cex", "cex-18", "valid_tovrin_p4_syntax").
?shown-violated("cex-18").

// 4. The bound: more than a tenth over is a violation; within a tenth is not; a better green run tightens it.
+figure("run_ms"). +amount(900). +amount(1000). +amount(1090). +amount(1150).
case-measured-green("lemma-3", "run_ms", 1000).
?baseline("lemma-3", "run_ms", 1000).
case-measured-green("lemma-3", "run_ms", 1090).
?!regressed("lemma-3", "run_ms").                               // 9 % over: within the cap
?!Violated(owes-time-bound("tovrin.runner", "o1", "lemma-3", "run_ms")).
case-measured-green("lemma-3", "run_ms", 1150).
?regressed("lemma-3", "run_ms").                                // 15 % over
?Violated(owes-time-bound("tovrin.runner", "o1", "lemma-3", "run_ms")).
?baseline("lemma-3", "run_ms", 1000).                           // a worse run does not move the bound
?!Enabled(overrule-bound("b1", "lemma-3", "run_ms")).
?!Enabled(overrule-bound("tovrin.runner", "lemma-3", "run_ms")).   // the holder cannot clear its own violation
overrule-bound("or1", "lemma-3", "run_ms").
?!Violated(owes-time-bound("tovrin.runner", "o1", "lemma-3", "run_ms")).
case-measured-green("lemma-3", "run_ms", 900).
?baseline("lemma-3", "run_ms", 900).                            // a better green run is the bound from then on
